<!-- What the trimmer keeps of the lazy explorer (ADR 0252): its pages, which
     the router finds by reflection once the assembly is loaded. The host
     names no type of it (VARVE0006), so without this the trimmer would drop
     it whole. A part or a component is kept when a page names it, so one no
     page uses yet stays out of the lazy set (#355, 2026-11-24). Not the
     whole assembly: that would keep the decision ledger every assembly
     carries as generated types. -->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Varve.WebUi.Explorer">
    <namespace fullname="Varve.WebUi.Explorer.Pages" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
